1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,460
In the meantime, when so many thousands of the people had gathered together that they

2
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:12,260
were trampling one another, he began to say to his disciples first,

3
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:16,740
Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy.

4
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:21,720
Nothing is covered up that will not be revealed, or hidden that will not be known.

5
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:26,700
Therefore whatever you have said in the dark shall be heard in the light, and what you

6
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:31,200
have whispered in private rooms shall be proclaimed on the housetops.

7
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:39,940
I tell you, my friends, do not fear those who kill the body, and after that have nothing

8
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:41,160
more that they can do.

9
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:43,820
But I will warn you whom to fear.

10
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:48,760
Fear him who, after he has killed, has authority to cast into hell.

11
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,480
Yes, I tell you, fear him.

12
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:55,280
Are not five sparrows sold for two pennies?

13
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,580
And not one of them is forgotten before God.

14
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:02,140
Why, even the hairs of your head are all numbered.

15
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:03,820
Fear not.

16
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:07,500
You are of more value than many sparrows.

17
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:15,260
And I tell you, everyone who acknowledges me before men, the Son of Man also will acknowledge

18
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:17,120
before the angels of God.

19
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:22,640
But the one who denies me before men will be denied before the angels of God.

20
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:25,260
And everyone who speaks a word against me before the angels of God will be denied before

21
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:25,380
the angels of God.

22
00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:31,080
The Son of Man will be forgiven, but the one who blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will

23
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:32,260
not be forgiven.

24
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:39,120
And when they bring you before the synagogues, and the rulers, and the authorities, do not

25
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:44,940
be anxious about how you should defend yourself or what you should say, for the Holy Spirit

26
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:48,040
will teach you in that very hour what you ought to say.

27
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:50,400
Someone in the crowd said to him,

28
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:54,540
Teacher, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me.

29
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,300
But he said to him,

30
00:01:57,060 --> 00:02:01,040
Man, who made me a judge or arbitrator over you?

31
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:02,700
And he said to them,

32
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:07,220
Take care, and be on your guard against all covetousness.

33
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:11,640
For one's life does not consist in the abundance of his possessions.

34
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:14,340
And he told them a parable, saying,

35
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,360
The land of a rich man produced plentifully.

36
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:23,400
And he thought to himself, What shall I do, for I have nowhere to store my crops?

37
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:24,760
And he said,

38
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:25,260
I am the land of the rich, and I have nowhere to store my crops.

39
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:26,400
I will do this.

40
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:31,760
I will tear down my barns and build larger ones, and there I will store all my grain

41
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:32,520
and my goods.

42
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:38,700
And I will say to my soul, Soul, you have ample goods laid up for many years.

43
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:42,560
Relax, eat, drink, be merry.

44
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:49,860
But God said to him, Fool, this night your soul is required of you, and the things you

45
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:52,180
have prepared, whose will they be?

46
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:55,180
So is the one who lays up treachery.

47
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:58,500
So is the one who lays up treachery for himself, and is not rich toward God.

48
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,600
And he said to his disciples,

49
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:07,020
Therefore I tell you, do not be anxious about your life, what you will eat, nor about your

50
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,340
body, what you will put on.

51
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:12,000
For life is more than food, and the body more than clothing.

52
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:14,040
Consider the ravens.

53
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:16,520
They neither sow nor reap.

54
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:19,240
They have neither storehouse nor barn.

55
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,420
And yet God feeds them.

56
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:25,180
Of how much more value are you than the birds?

57
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:30,540
And which of you, by being anxious, can add a single hour to his span of life?

58
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:36,800
If then you are not able to do as small a thing as that, why are you anxious about the

59
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,160
rest?

60
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:40,280
Consider the lilies, how they grow.

61
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,380
They neither toil nor spin.

62
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:47,800
Yet I tell you, even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.

63
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:53,560
But if God so clothes the grass, which is alive in the field today and tomorrow is thrown

64
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:54,180
into the oven,

65
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:58,840
How much more will he clothe you, O you of little faith?

66
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:04,160
And do not seek what you are to eat and what you are to drink, nor be worried.

67
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:10,020
For all the nations of the world seek after these things, and your Father knows that you

68
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:10,680
need them.

69
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,600
Instead, seek his kingdom, and these things will be added to you.

70
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:21,800
Fear not, little flock, for it is your Father's good pleasure to give you the kingdom.

71
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,600
Sell your possessions.

72
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,200
And give to the needy.

73
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:30,400
Provide yourselves with moneybags that do not grow old, with a treasure in the heavens

74
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:35,620
that does not fail, where no thief approaches and no moth destroys.

75
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:39,880
For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.

76
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:44,220
Stay dressed for action, and keep your lamps burning.

77
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:49,120
And be like men who are waiting for their master to come home from the wedding feast,

78
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:53,280
so that they may open the door to him at once when he comes and knocks.

79
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,480
Blessed are those servants whom the master finds awake when he comes.

80
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:03,760
Truly I say to you, he will dress himself for service and have them recline at table,

81
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,780
and he will come and serve them.

82
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:12,020
If he comes in the second watch or in the third and finds them awake, blessed are those

83
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:12,420
servants.

84
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:18,380
But know this, that if the master of the house had known at what hour the thief was coming,

85
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:21,300
he would not have left his house to be broken into.

86
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,580
You also must be ready.

87
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:27,460
For the Son of Man is coming at an hour you do not expect.

88
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:29,000
Peter said,

89
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:33,560
Lord, are you telling this parable for us or for all?

90
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,360
And the Lord said,

91
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:40,780
Who then is the faithful and wise manager, whom his master will set over his household

92
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:43,480
to give them their portion of food at the proper time?

93
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:48,480
Blessed is that servant whom his master will find so doing when he comes.

94
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:52,620
Truly I say to you, he will set him over all his possessions.

95
00:05:53,600 --> 00:06:00,000
But if that servant says to himself, My master is delayed in coming, and begins to beat

96
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:05,800
the male and female servants, and to eat and drink and get drunk, the master of that servant

97
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:11,160
will come on a day when he does not expect him, and at an hour he does not know, and

98
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:14,560
will cut him in pieces and put him with the unfaithful.

99
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:20,580
And that servant who knew his master's will, but did not get ready or act according to

100
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,960
his will, will receive a severe beating.

101
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:28,620
But the one who did not know, and did what deserved a beating, will receive a light beating.

102
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:33,200
Everyone to whom much was given, of him much will be required.

103
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:37,420
And from him to whom they entrusted much, they will demand the more.

104
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:42,920
I came to cast fire on the earth, and would that it were already kindled.

105
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:49,880
I have a baptism to be baptized with, and how great is my distress until it is accomplished.

106
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:53,180
Do you think that I have come to give peace on earth?

107
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:56,000
No, I tell you, but rather division.

108
00:06:56,640 --> 00:07:02,620
For from now on, in one house there will be five divided, three against two, and two against three.

109
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:08,260
They will be divided father against son, and son against father, mother against daughter,

110
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:13,440
and daughter against mother, mother-in-law against her daughter-in-law, and daughter-in-law

111
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:14,680
against mother-in-law.

112
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:21,660
He also said to the crowds, When you see a cloud rising in the west, you say at once,

113
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,200
A shower is coming.

114
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,620
And so it happens.

115
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:27,460
And when you see the south wind blowing, you say,

116
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,300
There will be scorching heat.

117
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:30,540
And it happens.

118
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:31,940
You hypocrites!

119
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:37,680
You know how to interpret the appearance of earth and sky, but why do you not know how

120
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:39,480
to interpret the present time?

121
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:43,480
And why do you not judge for yourselves what is right?

122
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:49,680
As you go with your accuser before the magistrate, make an effort to settle with him on the way,

123
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:53,580
lest he drag you to the judge, and the judge hand you over to him.

124
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:56,560
And the judge hand you over to the officer, and the officer put you in prison.

125
00:07:57,200 --> 00:08:01,920
I tell you, you will never get out until you have paid the very last penny.

